WEBVTT

00:01:56.430 --> 00:02:01.130
"Why did he save us?
Where is he taking us?"

00:02:01.730 --> 00:02:03.290
That must be what you're thinking.

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:10.440
I know a few things
about this land.

00:02:14.810 --> 00:02:16.680
How may I help you, Sir?

00:02:17.150 --> 00:02:20.720
These are my guests. Would you
mind taking care of them?

00:02:20.720 --> 00:02:23.210
But of course! Please,
come this way.

00:02:25.090 --> 00:02:27.160
Rest here for a while.

00:02:27.160 --> 00:02:30.520
I will make the arrangements
necessary for you to return home.

00:02:33.460 --> 00:02:35.620
Make yourselves at home.

00:02:52.980 --> 00:02:55.420
My name is Miharu.

00:02:59.590 --> 00:03:02.620
Gowa... Yushiro...

00:03:15.510 --> 00:03:16.560
Stop!

00:03:19.180 --> 00:03:20.640
Don't bring back

00:03:22.710 --> 00:03:23.910
the terror!

00:03:25.880 --> 00:03:27.370
In that vision...

00:03:30.050 --> 00:03:34.460
In that vision, I heard your voice
speak to me inside my mind.

00:03:35.530 --> 00:03:39.480
I didn't want to let you do it again.

00:03:42.570 --> 00:03:45.660
The terror must not be repeated.

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:48.330
So what is this terror
that you keep...

00:03:50.570 --> 00:03:51.980
I'm sorry to keep you waiting.

00:03:51.980 --> 00:03:53.880
I've been able to reach them.

00:03:53.880 --> 00:03:56.350
Your friends should be
coming soon.

00:04:00.880 --> 00:04:02.370
Go.

00:04:07.320 --> 00:04:11.560
I'll see you again. I'm sure of it.

00:04:15.330 --> 00:04:17.270
We'll meet again.

00:04:19.840 --> 00:04:20.930
I see.

00:04:22.670 --> 00:04:24.660
Thank you for your hospitality.

00:04:34.250 --> 00:04:38.240
It appears there are some
complex issues with him.

00:04:41.560 --> 00:04:45.760
I've done nothing to incur
your wrath!

00:04:45.760 --> 00:04:49.320
No, like I was saying, we are just
looking for someone!

00:04:50.400 --> 00:04:51.740
Captain Ataka!

00:04:51.740 --> 00:04:53.230
Yushiro!

00:05:06.550 --> 00:05:08.590
There's not much time
until we take off.

00:05:08.590 --> 00:05:09.950
Are we really going to
make the flight?

00:05:09.950 --> 00:05:11.420
Of course, we will!

00:05:11.420 --> 00:05:14.890
Come on, you were actually there.

00:05:14.890 --> 00:05:17.030
Someone interrupted the
public channel

00:05:17.030 --> 00:05:19.630
of the multinational forces
radio traffic,

00:05:19.630 --> 00:05:21.960
and told us where we
could find you.

00:05:22.470 --> 00:05:24.630
What was this about, Captain?

00:05:27.840 --> 00:05:29.470
What about that girl?

00:05:32.640 --> 00:05:35.010
Oh well, Captain Kaburagi,

00:05:35.010 --> 00:05:37.950
at least we were able to get hold
of Captain Gowa, right.

00:05:38.850 --> 00:05:41.280
The roads here are atrocious,
so you have to be careful.

00:05:41.280 --> 00:05:43.390
Please tell me that sooner,
Captain!

00:05:43.390 --> 00:05:44.880
Well...

00:05:46.720 --> 00:05:49.920
I'm sorry about leaving
without permission.

00:06:05.240 --> 00:06:08.270
Now, let's talk about Belgistan.

00:06:08.880 --> 00:06:14.280
It appears we failed in capturing
Gowa's invitator.

00:06:14.280 --> 00:06:19.520
What about the invitator you're
responsible for, Councilman Meth?

00:06:20.060 --> 00:06:25.460
An agent in Akura has informed
me Miharu is back in our custody.

00:06:25.460 --> 00:06:30.200
Well, at least we were able to
avoid losing all our cards.

00:06:31.330 --> 00:06:33.600
We have more pressing
issues at hand.

00:06:33.600 --> 00:06:37.110
Like how parts of the Fake have
fallen into the hands of Gowa.

00:06:37.110 --> 00:06:42.010
Yes, XF-4's artificial
muscle tissues.

00:06:42.010 --> 00:06:45.750
We can't let them take it
back to Japan.

00:06:45.750 --> 00:06:48.080
Measures are already in
place to prevent that.

00:06:56.990 --> 00:06:59.060
You can make your case to me
when we return to Japan!

00:06:59.060 --> 00:07:01.530
We're going to the rear staging
area now! Move out!

00:07:01.530 --> 00:07:03.020
Yes, Sir!

00:07:12.280 --> 00:07:13.710
Captain Gowa!

00:07:13.710 --> 00:07:15.200
Yes, Sir!

00:07:24.750 --> 00:07:28.690
I wonder if the C&C vehicles that
took off ahead of us are all right?

00:07:28.690 --> 00:07:30.990
They had a head start.

00:07:30.990 --> 00:07:34.430
They should be arriving at the
rear staging area before we do.

00:07:34.430 --> 00:07:39.040
Geez, they might get sucked
into fighting Belgistan forces

00:07:39.040 --> 00:07:40.770
that haven't lowered
their arms yet.

00:07:40.770 --> 00:07:42.510
They're well aware of the risk.

00:07:42.510 --> 00:07:45.910
I guess they just couldn't stand to
part with their precious hotrod.

00:07:54.120 --> 00:07:56.520
The command vehicles
haven't arrived yet?

00:07:56.520 --> 00:07:58.350
I hope they didn't really
run across guerrillas!

00:08:03.490 --> 00:08:06.900
It could be worse. We do
have the TA's with us.

00:08:06.900 --> 00:08:09.600
We also have backups of
the combat records.

00:08:09.600 --> 00:08:13.070
We cannot allow any further
delays in our flight schedule.

00:08:13.070 --> 00:08:15.510
I'm well aware of that, but still...

00:08:15.510 --> 00:08:18.670
I'll have another flight
made out for them.

00:08:19.210 --> 00:08:20.700
Company Commander!

00:08:25.550 --> 00:08:27.780
Guerrillas really attacked you?!

00:08:28.950 --> 00:08:33.220
You really put this 1.5 billion yen
vehicle through the wringer.

00:08:35.460 --> 00:08:38.160
I'm very proud of you!
You did a good job!

00:08:38.160 --> 00:08:40.960
You didn't return fire even after
being pounded about like this.

00:08:40.960 --> 00:08:42.490
Major...

00:08:44.770 --> 00:08:48.070
Time to head home.
Everyone onboard!

00:08:51.040 --> 00:08:55.310
So, you need me to get that
package back from the SSDF?

00:08:55.850 --> 00:08:57.710
This situation calls for
a rapid response.

00:08:57.710 --> 00:09:00.650
We must find some way of
grounding them.

00:09:01.250 --> 00:09:03.990
Understood. We still have time.

00:09:03.990 --> 00:09:05.720
Leave it to me.

00:09:08.830 --> 00:09:12.200
What?! What do you mean,
"inspect the luggage"?!

00:09:12.200 --> 00:09:14.530
It's an order from base
headquarters.

00:09:14.530 --> 00:09:17.830
In any case, please stand
by where you are now.

00:09:17.830 --> 00:09:19.460
Just wait a minute here!

00:09:20.400 --> 00:09:21.170
Yeah, I know...

00:09:21.170 --> 00:09:22.710
Colonel Hayakawa!

00:09:22.710 --> 00:09:26.240
I've been given instructions from
the tower to delay our departure

00:09:26.240 --> 00:09:28.800
because they need to inspect
our equipment.

00:09:29.450 --> 00:09:30.850
Inspect our equipment?!

00:09:32.780 --> 00:09:35.620
Do you think they're after the
sample from the enemy TA's?

00:09:36.450 --> 00:09:37.990
An inspection?

00:09:37.990 --> 00:09:42.560
Even if it's the Americans, we can't
let them access that sample.

00:09:42.560 --> 00:09:44.630
I'll go and negotiate.

00:09:44.630 --> 00:09:46.930
If we get in a crunch, go ahead
and take off without me.

00:09:48.260 --> 00:09:50.760
Do you plan on staying behind?

00:09:52.570 --> 00:09:53.830
Mr. Kiyoharu?

00:09:55.110 --> 00:09:58.780
I've been tipped off that the
US Forces are interested

00:09:58.780 --> 00:10:01.380
in obtaining secrets
regarding our TA's.

00:10:01.380 --> 00:10:03.510
We need to prevent that no
matter what happens.

00:10:03.510 --> 00:10:05.110
We're all ready for take off!

00:10:05.850 --> 00:10:07.110
Where are you going?

00:10:11.760 --> 00:10:15.160
By order of General Wayne, we're
to inspect your cargo.

00:10:15.160 --> 00:10:18.260
The inside of this aircraft is
considered to be Japanese soil.

00:10:18.260 --> 00:10:22.250
Not even General Wayne has the
authority to search it.

00:10:24.030 --> 00:10:26.630
I will mention this to
General Wayne myself.

00:10:27.570 --> 00:10:29.270
Can I borrow your radio please?

00:10:30.070 --> 00:10:31.810
My brother understands
the risk he's taking.

00:10:31.810 --> 00:10:33.510
We need to take off now.

00:10:33.510 --> 00:10:37.380
But we won't receive assistance
from the tower.

00:10:37.380 --> 00:10:39.450
You can fly without instructions
from the tower.

00:10:39.450 --> 00:10:42.010
The Americans are after the
secrets of the TA's.

00:10:42.590 --> 00:10:45.280
We can't let them just walk in
and take them from us.

00:10:45.860 --> 00:10:47.560
Kiyoharu Gowa,

00:10:47.560 --> 00:10:51.630
I have final say over any and all
activities conducted on this base.

00:10:51.630 --> 00:10:56.070
My orders were issued with the
authority granted by US
Central Command HQ,

00:10:56.070 --> 00:10:57.900
and I'm not about to retract them.

00:10:57.900 --> 00:11:00.840
I understand what you
are saying, General.

00:11:00.840 --> 00:11:02.940
Captain, this is Kiyoharu.

00:11:02.940 --> 00:11:06.080
I've confirmed the orders
issued by General Wayne.

00:11:06.080 --> 00:11:08.910
The orders are based on
US prerogatives only.

00:11:08.910 --> 00:11:11.080
They have nothing to do
with the United Nations.

00:11:11.080 --> 00:11:15.650
The JSSDF is under no obligation
to heed such unreasonable orders.

00:11:15.650 --> 00:11:18.290
There you have it, General Wayne.

00:11:18.290 --> 00:11:21.020
If you wish to impede
our departure,

00:11:21.020 --> 00:11:24.930
I suggest you take it up through
diplomatic channels.

00:11:24.930 --> 00:11:26.790
Through diplomatic channels?!

00:11:27.430 --> 00:11:31.100
SC32001, we have not granted
you permission to take off.

00:11:31.100 --> 00:11:34.400
You are to shut down your
engines immediately!

00:11:34.400 --> 00:11:39.400
This is SC32001. We will take off
as an aircraft registered to Japan.

00:11:40.440 --> 00:11:42.880
What about your brother?

00:11:43.580 --> 00:11:47.910
Take off now before they place
obstacles on the runway! Hurry!

00:12:08.540 --> 00:12:10.440
They've started taxiing?!

00:12:11.540 --> 00:12:13.940
Right on schedule,
General Wayne.

00:12:18.280 --> 00:12:19.450
No runway lights!

00:12:19.450 --> 00:12:20.610
The hell with it!

00:12:35.030 --> 00:12:37.930
Currently we are flying at an
altitude of 24,000 feet.

00:12:37.930 --> 00:12:40.070
We just left Belgistan airspace.

00:12:40.070 --> 00:12:42.770
We're finally out of Belgistan.

00:12:43.210 --> 00:12:45.580
It's nice to be able to relax.

00:12:45.580 --> 00:12:47.410
It may be too soon for that.

00:12:47.410 --> 00:12:49.780
We are now in Armekistan
airspace.

00:12:49.780 --> 00:12:52.650
Unlike the other
neighboring nations,

00:12:52.650 --> 00:12:56.280
Armekistan supported Belgistan's
hard line to the bitter end.

00:13:02.260 --> 00:13:05.350
I think it's about time you came
clean with us, Captain.

00:13:05.930 --> 00:13:09.330
Captain Kitazawa,
you're scaring me!

00:13:09.330 --> 00:13:12.770
I'm sorry, but would you remain
quiet for a while, Lieutenant?

00:13:14.700 --> 00:13:16.940
First, it was a dance in the
middle of a war zone.

00:13:16.940 --> 00:13:19.580
Then, there was the car
chase in the city.

00:13:19.580 --> 00:13:22.110
Too many things don't
make sense.

00:13:22.110 --> 00:13:24.200
What was that dance about?

00:13:24.710 --> 00:13:26.270
Why were they after you?

00:13:29.790 --> 00:13:32.220
Captain, the ICAO is
getting a call sign.

00:13:32.220 --> 00:13:34.280
On the international open
communications channel?

00:13:35.290 --> 00:13:38.560
...are intruding into our
nation's airspace.

00:13:38.560 --> 00:13:44.070
Change heading to 315 degrees,
and lower altitude to 3,000 feet.

00:13:44.070 --> 00:13:46.090
Airspace intrusion?!

00:13:46.900 --> 00:13:51.610
Repeat. This is the Armekistan
Airspace Defense Corps 2nd
interception sortie,

00:13:51.610 --> 00:13:54.940
IF-2101 and IF-2102.

00:13:55.480 --> 00:13:59.740
You are intruding into our nation's
airspace. Change heading to...

00:14:00.680 --> 00:14:02.350
Captain Kitazawa...

00:14:02.350 --> 00:14:06.420
Company Commander, I aim
to trust my team members.

00:14:06.420 --> 00:14:07.690
But in order to do that,

00:14:07.690 --> 00:14:12.250
I must have Captain Gowa relieve
the lingering suspicions we have.

00:14:18.870 --> 00:14:21.960
This issue goes beyond the
actions of Captain Gowa.

00:14:22.610 --> 00:14:26.510
An overseas deployment pushed
through without regard to its
constitutionality.

00:14:26.510 --> 00:14:31.480
I see a company rejecting law and
order in pursuit of its interests!

00:14:31.480 --> 00:14:37.040
Were Captain Gowa's actions
based on Gowa's corporate ethics?

00:14:53.040 --> 00:14:54.940
This is the co-pilot.

00:14:56.140 --> 00:14:58.540
Colonel Hayakawa, please come
to the cockpit right away!

00:15:02.880 --> 00:15:11.620
I repeat, this is JSSDF Strategic
Airlift Group aircraft SC32001.

00:15:15.890 --> 00:15:20.800
We are flying on a flight path
approved by the United Nations.

00:15:22.830 --> 00:15:26.440
It's no good! They won't listen
to a word we're saying!

00:15:26.440 --> 00:15:30.010
Two fighters. They look
like Sukhoi 37's.

00:15:30.010 --> 00:15:32.710
They're tailing us closely from
above at 5 o'clock and 7 o'clock.

00:15:32.710 --> 00:15:34.810
Try the IFF again!

00:15:34.810 --> 00:15:36.300
Yes, Sir!

00:15:38.350 --> 00:15:39.920
What's wrong?

00:15:39.920 --> 00:15:43.790
Colonel, we have two Armekistan
fighters tailing us,

00:15:43.790 --> 00:15:48.060
and they're telling us we need to
change our heading to southwest.

00:15:48.060 --> 00:15:51.790
But I thought our flight plan was
approved by the United Nations?

00:15:51.790 --> 00:15:54.100
That's what I keep telling them.

00:15:54.100 --> 00:15:56.070
They're not responding
to the IFF system!

00:15:56.070 --> 00:15:57.200
Not responding?!

00:15:57.200 --> 00:15:58.630
What does that mean?

00:15:58.630 --> 00:16:03.230
They're not responding to the
aircraft identification code.

00:16:04.270 --> 00:16:07.870
In other words, the fighters are
concealing their true identity?

00:16:10.150 --> 00:16:11.410
What's happened?

00:16:12.180 --> 00:16:14.020
Armekistan Air Force aircraft.

00:16:14.020 --> 00:16:17.050
They're demanding that we
change our heading.

00:16:17.050 --> 00:16:18.420
We can't do that!

00:16:18.420 --> 00:16:21.990
This aircraft is proceeding on an
officially sanctioned flight path.

00:16:21.990 --> 00:16:23.490
Go ahead and ignore them.

00:16:23.490 --> 00:16:24.930
I don't think that's an option.

00:16:25.530 --> 00:16:27.030
A warning shot?!

00:16:27.030 --> 00:16:28.720
They're serious out there!

00:16:29.330 --> 00:16:31.400
The trouble at takeoff
and now this.

00:16:31.400 --> 00:16:36.040
Someone clearly wants to block
us from returning to Japan.

00:16:36.040 --> 00:16:38.440
You're hiding something,
aren't you?!

00:16:42.110 --> 00:16:44.850
Gunfire impact! Shutting
down engine one!

00:16:44.850 --> 00:16:48.410
Shut down fuel line!
Engine two maximum power!

00:16:53.960 --> 00:16:59.860
This flight is carrying samples of
the enemy TA's artificial muscle.

00:17:00.400 --> 00:17:01.990
What? A thing like that?

00:17:02.900 --> 00:17:05.030
They're probably after that.

00:17:05.030 --> 00:17:06.070
But Colonel,

00:17:06.070 --> 00:17:09.570
you realize how vital it is to
Japan's interests to retain it!

00:17:09.570 --> 00:17:11.840
So you're saying that fighter is...

00:17:11.840 --> 00:17:15.850
Yes. While those aircraft might be
the property of Armekistan,

00:17:15.850 --> 00:17:19.800
they're taking orders from the
ones who controlled those TA's.

00:17:20.820 --> 00:17:25.950
I see. They intend to reclaim their
secret after forcing us to land,

00:17:26.790 --> 00:17:30.250
and then deal with us so that no
one will find out what happened.

00:17:31.090 --> 00:17:32.900
Can't you return fire?

00:17:32.900 --> 00:17:35.770
You've got to be kidding.
We have no armaments!

00:17:35.770 --> 00:17:37.300
We'll have to surrender to them.

00:17:37.300 --> 00:17:43.340
If we do that, there's no doubt
we would disappear.

00:17:43.340 --> 00:17:47.210
Captain, can you open the cargo
bay hatch while you're in flight?

00:17:47.210 --> 00:17:48.950
Yes, I can, but that's suicidal!

00:17:48.950 --> 00:17:53.720
Our speed and altitude will drop
fast since we've lost an engine.

00:17:53.720 --> 00:17:56.390
Colonel Hayakawa,
let's fight back.

00:17:56.390 --> 00:17:58.250
We have armaments. Our TA's!

00:18:00.390 --> 00:18:04.130
We'll drop a TA, tethered by wires,
from the rear cargo hatch,

00:18:04.130 --> 00:18:05.930
and take them by surprise.

00:18:05.930 --> 00:18:06.990
It's possible!

00:18:08.400 --> 00:18:14.030
Our opponents are fighters! Who
can pull off a circus act like that?

00:18:15.870 --> 00:18:20.280
If that's our only choice,
then I would like to...

00:18:20.280 --> 00:18:21.610
I'll do it.

00:18:23.180 --> 00:18:24.670
I will.

00:18:27.250 --> 00:18:29.680
This is a mission only Captain
Gowa can do.

00:18:30.290 --> 00:18:32.310
You realize that, don't you, Major?

00:18:33.960 --> 00:18:36.050
We're counting on you,
Captain Gowa!

00:18:38.190 --> 00:18:39.680
Yes, Sir.

00:18:44.270 --> 00:18:49.300
The enemy will probably attempt
another volley of warning shots.

00:18:49.910 --> 00:18:51.310
That will be our
opportunity to strike.

00:18:51.310 --> 00:18:56.080
Understood. We'll estimate their
position based on their fire.

00:18:56.080 --> 00:18:58.920
We don't have a fire control radar
available, what do we do?

00:18:58.920 --> 00:19:02.620
We'll substitute for it with a laser
range finder, and link it to the TA.

00:19:02.620 --> 00:19:03.420
Armament?

00:19:03.420 --> 00:19:05.020
25mm machine gun.

00:19:05.020 --> 00:19:08.160
The trajectory characteristics of
high altitude shooting are in.

00:19:08.160 --> 00:19:10.990
The reaction time is to be set 620
milliseconds, correct?

00:19:10.990 --> 00:19:14.760
Yes, I've given you all the data
our researchers have produced.

00:19:14.760 --> 00:19:16.570
This will help us a lot.

00:19:16.570 --> 00:19:22.530
But in return, I'd like a copy of
Yushiro's combat records later on.

00:19:25.470 --> 00:19:27.480
This is nuts!

00:19:27.480 --> 00:19:32.150
Even though we're slow, we're
still flying at over 400km per hour.

00:19:32.150 --> 00:19:34.280
I realize that this is a
very risky plan,

00:19:34.280 --> 00:19:37.580
but Captain Gowa just might
be able to pull it off.

00:19:38.550 --> 00:19:40.250
Focus One, booting up!

00:19:41.990 --> 00:19:44.530
The cargo area will depressurize
quickly once that bay opens.

00:19:44.530 --> 00:19:47.000
All crew, evacuate once
the TA is up!

00:19:54.800 --> 00:19:56.310
Are you sure about this, Captain?!

00:19:56.310 --> 00:19:59.580
We're going to do it! You heard
what Colonel Hayakawa said!

00:19:59.580 --> 00:20:02.510
This is Focus One. Ready to go.

00:20:02.510 --> 00:20:04.550
Another warning from the
Armekistan fighters.

00:20:04.550 --> 00:20:07.980
They said unless we respond in
sixty seconds, they will shoot.

00:20:07.980 --> 00:20:12.110
All settings ready. We'll start five
seconds before the fighters shoot.

00:20:14.160 --> 00:20:16.290
Focus One, Captain Gowa...

00:20:16.290 --> 00:20:17.060
45...
Focus One, Captain Gowa...

00:20:17.060 --> 00:20:17.790
45...
The success of this operation
hinges on being able to trust you.

00:20:17.790 --> 00:20:20.830
The success of this operation
hinges on being able to trust you.

00:20:20.830 --> 00:20:21.430
That's why I'm going to put faith
in you. I'm counting on you.

00:20:21.430 --> 00:20:22.600
40...
That's why I'm going to put faith
in you. I'm counting on you.

00:20:22.600 --> 00:20:23.290
That's why I'm going to put faith
in you. I'm counting on you.

00:20:23.930 --> 00:20:26.400
Thank you for saying that.

00:20:27.700 --> 00:20:30.910
At thirty seconds to drop, we'll
drop down to 300km.

00:20:30.910 --> 00:20:33.140
Is that the stall threshold
of the Sukhois?

00:20:33.140 --> 00:20:34.610
That's the best we can do.

00:20:34.610 --> 00:20:36.610
The target's maneuverability
will decrease, but even then,

00:20:36.610 --> 00:20:40.720
the TA's window for aiming
will only increase by 15%.

00:20:40.720 --> 00:20:41.320
We still only have one shot at this.

00:20:41.320 --> 00:20:42.890
20...
We still only have one shot at this.

00:20:42.890 --> 00:20:44.650
If we fail in this raid,

00:20:45.590 --> 00:20:46.290
there won't be a second chance.

00:20:46.290 --> 00:20:47.080
15...
there won't be a second chance.

00:20:51.330 --> 00:20:52.360
10...

00:20:52.360 --> 00:20:53.300
9...

00:20:53.300 --> 00:20:53.530
8...

00:20:53.530 --> 00:20:54.230
We're still counting down?!
8...

00:20:54.230 --> 00:20:55.230
We're still counting down?!
7...

00:20:55.230 --> 00:20:55.530
We're still counting down?!
6...

00:20:55.530 --> 00:20:56.500
Open the rear hatch!
6...

00:21:05.540 --> 00:21:07.040
Jettisoning Focus One.

00:21:07.040 --> 00:21:08.530
Roger.

00:21:24.260 --> 00:21:25.330
He missed?!

00:21:25.330 --> 00:21:28.130
Trouble. We can't turn around.

00:21:57.630 --> 00:21:59.320
I don't believe it.

00:22:13.180 --> 00:22:17.250
I understand the TA team will be
arriving at Kagamigahara shortly.

00:22:17.250 --> 00:22:20.080
Japan will be enveloped
by commotion soon.

00:22:20.080 --> 00:22:22.020
That would seem to be the case.

00:22:22.020 --> 00:22:24.650
It begins now. Doesn't it?

00:22:29.080 --> 00:22:33.900
Hark

00:22:35.060 --> 00:22:40.350
It's time I journey

00:22:43.880 --> 00:22:51.020
Break apart my heart

00:22:51.190 --> 00:22:57.550
For crimson sadness

00:22:57.880 --> 00:23:05.060
Pours out from it

00:23:05.270 --> 00:23:08.980
I can only, oh

00:23:09.090 --> 00:23:12.170
Close my eyes, oh

00:23:12.260 --> 00:23:17.780
I pray, let this break apart

00:23:33.000 --> 00:23:36.880
I can only, oh

00:23:36.970 --> 00:23:40.030
Close my eyes, oh

00:23:40.100 --> 00:23:45.230
I pray, let this break apart

00:23:46.760 --> 00:23:53.210
I beg you, be by my side

00:24:01.320 --> 00:24:03.680
I've come back to Japan.

00:24:04.550 --> 00:24:07.780
But why do I feel as if I'm
not welcome here?

00:24:08.620 --> 00:24:10.590
Why does it feel so cold?

00:24:11.690 --> 00:24:15.890
This is my home, where
I was born.

00:24:16.830 --> 00:24:18.570
Each of the three realms

00:24:18.570 --> 00:24:21.040
Overflowing with sentiments
and memories

00:24:21.040 --> 00:24:24.270
All have become but harsh
worlds of desire and pathos.

00:24:24.970 --> 00:24:28.880
Where am I supposed to be?
